        "original_id": "a4c80fd2-7947-5e32-87d3-22483e8c3f20",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Manettia, Fragaria, strawberries\n- People: Saverio Manetti, Carolus Linnaeus\n- Viruses: Strawberry crinkle virus (SCV)\n- Families: Rubiaceae, Rosaceae, Rhabdoviridae\n\nFacts:\n- Manettia is a genus of flowering plants in the family Rubiaceae.\n- Fragaria is a genus of flowering plants in the family Rosaceae and is commonly known as strawberries for its edible fruits.\n- Carolus Linnaeus named the plant genus Manettia in honor of Saverio Manetti.\n- Strawberry crinkle virus (SCV) is a plant virus in the family Rhabdoviridae that infects plants of the genus Fragaria, commonly called strawberries.",
